title: Library_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("library_intro")>>
    Dex: The library. So quiet I can hear my own nervous sweating.
    Ms. Hush: Shhh.
    Dex: I didn't say anything!
    Ms. Hush: Shhhhh.
    <<flag library_intro>>
<<elseif flagged("a1_hush_distracted") and not flagged("won_ivy")>>
    Dex: Ms. Hush is still hunting through the card catalogue. Drawer by drawer. Muttering.
<<endif>>
===

title: LibraryExit_Look
---
Dex: Back out to the quad, where talking is legal.
===
title: LibraryExit_Use
---
<<go campus from_library>>
===

title: FrontDesk_Look
---
Dex: The front desk. A bell nobody would dare ring, and a stack of returns taller than me.
===
title: FrontDesk_Use
---
<<if flagged("a1_hush_distracted")>>
    Dex: Ms. Hush is busy. I could ring the bell. I could. I won't. I'm not a monster.
<<else>>
    Dex: I reach for the bell. Ms. Hush turns her head very slowly. I put my hand back in my pocket.
<<endif>>
===

title: Hush_Look
---
<<if flagged("a1_hush_distracted") and not flagged("won_ivy")>>
    Dex: Ms. Hush, yanking open catalogue drawers, hunting for whatever dared to ring in her library.
<<else>>
    Dex: Ms. Hush, head librarian. Rumour says she shushed a fire alarm into silence.
<<endif>>
===
title: Hush_Talk
---
<<if flagged("won_ivy")>>
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) I heard about the Talent Round. Poetry and interpretive dance. Hmph.
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) ...I would have liked to see that.
<<elseif not flagged("met_hush")>>
    Dex: Hi! I'm looking for...
    Ms. Hush: Shhh. This is a library. Talking is for the cafeteria. Notes are for the desperate.
    <<flag met_hush>>
<<elseif flagged("a1_hush_distracted")>>
    Ms. Hush: (rifling drawers) Somewhere in this catalogue, something RANG. In MY library. Between D and F, I can feel it.
<<else>>
    Ms. Hush: Shhh. (whispering) If you must speak, speak like a moth.
<<endif>>
<<jump A1_Hush_Menu>>
===
title: A1_Hush_Menu
---
-> (whisper) Ask what's upstairs <<if not flagged("a1_cb_puddle")>>
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) The upper stacks. Closed after dark. Except to that Thorne boy and his so-called slam.
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) He says his verse is deep. The puddle on my front steps is deeper, and it shows more reflection.
    Dex: (Ha. "So is the puddle on the library steps, and it shows more reflection." Filing that one away.)
    <<flag a1_cb_puddle>>
    <<jump A1_Hush_Menu>>
-> (whisper) Ask about Percival Thorne <<if flagged("a1_cb_puddle") and not flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) Thirty-seven wins. He doesn't win with rhymes. He wins with insults, and nobody ever has an answer ready.
    <<jump A1_Hush_Menu>>
-> (whisper) Ask to go up the ladder <<if not flagged("a1_hush_distracted")>>
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) No.
    Dex: (whispering) Not even for a minute?
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) I've been watching that ladder for thirty years. It has never once gone anywhere without my say-so.
    <<jump A1_Hush_Menu>>
-> (whisper) Ask about Ivy <<if flagged("met_ivy") and not flagged("won_ivy")>>
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) That girl has read every book on the Feelings shelf. Twice. She returns them on time. I'd die for her.
    <<jump A1_Hush_Menu>>
-> (whisper) Ask about the founder <<if not flagged("a1_hush_founder")>>
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) Augustus Plumworth built this library so students would have one quiet place. He'd hate what they did to his statue.
    <<flag a1_hush_founder>>
    <<jump A1_Hush_Menu>>
-> (whisper) Ask what happens if you talk loudly
    Ms. Hush: (whispering) Nobody knows. Nobody has ever finished the sentence.
    <<jump A1_Hush_Menu>>
-> Back away quietly
    Ms. Hush: Shhh.
===
title: Hush_Note
---
Ms. Hush: (reading it) "Circle YES or YES." Hmph. Passing notes is the only civilised way to flirt in here.
Ms. Hush: Deliver it yourself, young man. Quietly.
===
title: A1_Hush_GiveAlarm
---
Dex: Hand the head librarian a loud, ticking alarm clock? I'd be shushed out of existence. It needs to ring somewhere far away from me.
===

title: A1_Catalogue_Look
---
Dex: The card catalogue. Hundreds of tiny drawers. Ms. Hush knows every card in every one of them by heart.
===
title: A1_Catalogue_Use
---
Dex: I open a drawer. "Plumworth, Augustus. See also: Statues, Pigeons." Riveting. I shut it before Ms. Hush hears.
===
title: A1_Catalogue_Alarm
---
Dex: I set Boomer's alarm clock to go off in one minute, slip it into drawer E for Emergency, and stroll away. Whistling. No. Not whistling.
Dex: ...
Dex: RRRRRRRIIIIIIINNNNNNG!
Ms. Hush: WHAT. IS. THAT.
Dex: Ms. Hush flies across the room to the card catalogue and starts pulling out drawers. It might take her all night.
Dex: Nobody's watching the ladder.
<<take boomer_alarm>>
<<flag a1_hush_distracted>>
===

title: A1_Ladder_Look
---
Dex: A rolling ladder up to the mezzanine. A small sign: UPPER STACKS, STAFF ONLY AFTER DARK.
===
title: A1_Ladder_Use
---
<<if flagged("a1_hush_distracted")>>
    Dex: Up I go. Quietly. The ladder squeaks once. Ms. Hush is too busy with the drawers to notice.
    <<go library_stacks from_library>>
<<else>>
    Ms. Hush: (without turning around) The upper stacks are closed after dark, young man. And that ladder squeaks.
    Dex: She didn't even look. She just knew. I'll need to give her something else to listen to.
<<endif>>
===

title: Shelves_Look
---
Dex: Poetry, philosophy, and one shelf just labelled "Feelings". Ivy has clearly read all of it.
===
title: Shelves_Use
---
<<if not flagged("read_poetry")>>
    Dex: "Poems to Read Aloud (But Never Will)." Every page has a sticky note in tiny writing. Somebody loves this book.
    <<flag read_poetry>>
<<else>>
    Dex: I'm not much of a reader. I'm more of a... looker-at-the-pictures.
<<endif>>
===

title: ReadingTable_Look
---
Dex: A reading table under a green lamp, covered in open poetry books and pencil notes.
===
title: ReadingTable_Use
---
<<if flagged("a1_ivy_notebook")>>
    Dex: Ivy's notebook is back where it belongs. Open to "Ode to the Quiet Kid in the Back Row." It's actually really good.
    <<flag read_ivy_poem>>
<<else>>
    Dex: Pencils, erasers, a coffee ring, and a notebook-shaped gap in the dust. Somebody's notebook used to be here.
<<endif>>
===

title: Ivy_Look
---
<<if flagged("won_ivy")>>
    Dex: Ivy, sunglasses on, reading under her breath like she's rehearsing for the world.
<<else>>
    Dex: A girl in big round glasses, hugging a book like it's a shield. She hasn't looked up once.
<<endif>>
===
title: Ivy_Talk
---
<<if flagged("won_ivy")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) Partner! Meet me at the stage. Roxy's waiting.
<<elseif flagged("ivy_note")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) Hi, Dex. Nice handwriting, by the way.
<<else>>
    Dex: Hi! I'm Dex. Do you, uh, have a talent?
    Ms. Hush: SHHHH!
    Ivy: ...
    Dex: She's too scared to even whisper with Ms. Hush around. Maybe I should write it down.
    <<flag met_ivy>>
<<endif>>
<<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
===
title: A1_Ivy_Menu
---
-> Ask her name <<if not flagged("ivy_note") and not flagged("a1_ivy_name")>>
    Dex: She silently turns her book so I can see the name inside the cover. IVY. Then she turns it back.
    Ms. Hush: Shhh.
    Dex: I didn't SAY anything.
    <<flag a1_ivy_name>>
    <<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Ask what she's reading <<if not flagged("ivy_note")>>
    Dex: She tilts the cover toward me. POEMS. Then she hides behind it again.
    <<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Ask about her stage fright <<if flagged("ivy_note") and not flagged("a1_ivy_shades")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) I'd read my poem if I didn't have to see all those faces staring at me.
    Dex: (whispering) What if you couldn't see them?
    Ivy: (whispering) Like, with my eyes closed? Then I can't read the page, genius.
    <<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Ask about her notebook <<if flagged("ivy_note") and not flagged("a1_ivy_notebook")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) My poems are in it. All of them. I left it on the table for one minute.
    Ivy: (whispering) Percival Thorne took it up to the stacks. He says my poem is "derivative", and he's going to perform it at the Talent Round. As his.
    <<flag a1_heard_notebook>>
    <<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Ask about Percival <<if flagged("a1_heard_notebook") and not flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) He runs the Stacks Slam. Nobody beats him. He just insults people until they cry.
    Ivy: (whispering) The trick is having an answer for every insult. Nobody ever does.
    <<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Ask about her poem <<if flagged("ivy_note")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) It's called "Ode to the Quiet Kid in the Back Row." It's about... someone. Nobody. Me.
    <<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Ask about the Talent Round <<if flagged("ivy_note") and not flagged("won_ivy")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) Your partner. Me. On a stage. In front of everyone. I said yes, and now I want to lie down in a dark cupboard.
    <<jump A1_Ivy_Menu>>
-> Leave her to her book
    Ivy: (a tiny wave)
===
title: Ivy_GiveNote
---
<<if flagged("ivy_note")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) I already circled yes. Twice.
<<else>>
    Ivy: (reads it, tries not to smile, writes back)
    Dex: Her reply: "YES. I write poems. I've never read one out loud. When people stare at me, I freeze."
    Dex: "If I couldn't see them staring, maybe I could do it." P.S. "Nice handwriting."
    Dex: P.P.S. "Also, Percival Thorne stole my notebook. My poem's in it. He's up in the stacks."
    <<take note_for_ivy>>
    <<flag ivy_note>>
    <<flag met_ivy>>
    <<flag a1_heard_notebook>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Ivy_GiveSunglasses
---
<<if not flagged("ivy_note")>>
    Ivy: ...
    Dex: She thinks I'm a weirdo handing out sunglasses. She's not wrong. I should introduce myself first. Quietly.
<<elseif flagged("a1_ivy_shades")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) I've already got shades on. Two pairs would be a bit much. Even for me.
<<else>>
    Ivy: (puts them on) Oh. Oh! Everything's dark and blurry, except the page right in front of me.
    Ivy: (whispering) I can't see the crowd. I can do this. I can actually do this.
    <<take sunglasses>>
    <<flag a1_ivy_shades>>
    <<jump A1_Ivy_CheckWin>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A1_Ivy_GiveNotebook
---
<<if not flagged("ivy_note")>>
    Ivy: ...
    Dex: She stares at her notebook, then at me, like I'm a stranger who stole it. Which, from her side, I might be. A note first.
<<else>>
    Ivy: (hugging it) My notebook! You beat Percival? Nobody beats Percival!
    Dex: I had help. A cowgirl, a cook, a possum and a librarian.
    Ivy: (whispering) That's the best sentence I've ever heard.
    <<take ivy_notebook>>
    <<flag a1_ivy_notebook>>
    <<jump A1_Ivy_CheckWin>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A1_Ivy_CheckWin
---
<<if flagged("a1_ivy_shades") and flagged("a1_ivy_notebook")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) My poem, and a way to hide from the crowd. Okay. Okay!
    Ivy: Here, my bookmark. So you know I'm serious. Meet you at the stage, partner.
    <<give bookmark>>
    <<flag won_ivy>>
<<elseif flagged("a1_ivy_shades")>>
    Ivy: (whispering) But I can't read a poem I don't have. My notebook is still up in the stacks with Percival.
<<else>>
    Ivy: (whispering) I have my poem back. Now I just need to not see the hundred people staring at me.
<<endif>>
===
title: Ivy_ShowHat
---
Ivy: (whispering) Is that Lacey Rae's hat? Everybody's talking about you. Now I'm even more nervous.
===

title: A1_Stacks_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("a1_stacks_intro")>>
    Dex: The upper stacks. Dust, moonlight, three beanbags facing a microphone, and one guy in a beret, snapping his fingers at nobody.
    Percival Thorne: Ah. An audience. Finally, the universe apologises.
    <<flag a1_stacks_intro>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A1_LadderDown_Look
---
Dex: The ladder back down to the reading room. Mind the squeaky rung. All of them are the squeaky rung.
===
title: A1_LadderDown_Use
---
<<go library from_stacks>>
===
title: A1_Dusty_Look
---
Dex: Shelves of theses nobody has opened since 1962. "The Feelings of Turnips, Volume Four."
===
title: A1_Dusty_Use
---
<<if not flagged("a1_dusty_book")>>
    Dex: "Comebacks for Beginners." Every single page has been torn out. Somebody got here first.
    Dex: Guess I'll have to learn my comebacks from actual people. Ugh. Talking.
    <<flag a1_dusty_book>>
<<else>>
    Dex: More dust. I sneeze. Downstairs, I can hear Ms. Hush shushing the sneeze.
<<endif>>
===
title: A1_Chalk_Look
---
Dex: A chalkboard: "STACKS SLAM. Champion: P. THORNE. 37 wins, 0 losses." Thirty-seven little crying faces drawn underneath.
===
title: A1_Chalk_Use
---
<<if flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Dex: I add a tally under a new column: D. DOOLEY, 1. And a little cowboy hat.
<<else>>
    Dex: I could draw a mustache on the champion's name. But then I'd have to explain myself to a man in a beret.
<<endif>>
===
title: A1_Mic_Look
---
Dex: An open mic on a stand. Someone has written "PERCIVAL ONLY" on the stand. In calligraphy.
===
title: A1_Mic_Use
---
Percival Thorne: Do NOT touch the mic. The mic is a sacred instrument. And I just polished it.
===
title: A1_Bust_Look
---
Dex: A marble bust of founder Augustus Plumworth. Up here, he looks lonely. And dusty. Mostly dusty.
===
title: A1_Bust_Use
---
Dex: I dust off his nose with my sleeve. Augustus looks grateful. Or constipated. Marble is hard to read.
===
title: A1_Bust_Sunglasses
---
Dex: He'd look incredible in them. But Ivy needs these more than a man made of rock.
===

title: A1_Percival_Look
---
<<if flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Dex: Percival Thorne, sulking in a beanbag, beret pulled over his eyes. Thirty-seven and one.
<<else>>
    Dex: Black turtleneck, beret, a scarf in a heatwave. He's holding a notebook with a pressed daisy drawn on the cover. Ivy's notebook.
<<endif>>
===
title: A1_Percival_Talk
---
<<if flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Percival Thorne: Leave me. I'm processing my first loss. Through interpretive silence.
<<elseif not flagged("a1_met_percival")>>
    Percival Thorne: Percival Thorne. Poet. Slam champion. Thirty-seven wins, zero losses, and one very good scarf.
    Dex: Dex Dooley. Is that notebook yours?
    Percival Thorne: It is now. Some little mouse left it on the reading table. I'll be performing its best poem at the Talent Round. Lightly improved.
    Percival Thorne: By which I mean I crossed out her name and wrote mine.
    <<flag a1_met_percival>>
<<elseif flagged("a1_lost_slam")>>
    Percival Thorne: Back for another beating? Your comebacks are like your shirt, freshman. Loud and empty.
<<else>>
    Percival Thorne: Still here? I don't give autographs. Unless you have a pen.
<<endif>>
<<jump A1_Percival_Menu>>
===
title: A1_Percival_Menu
---
-> Ask him to give the notebook back <<if not flagged("a1_won_slam") and not flagged("a1_slam_rules")>>
    Percival Thorne: Slam law, freshman. Anything left in the Stacks belongs to the champion.
    Percival Thorne: Unless someone beats the champion in a slam-off. Which nobody ever has. Or ever will.
    Dex: How does a slam-off work?
    Percival Thorne: I insult you in verse. You answer with something better. Run out of answers and you lose.
    <<flag a1_slam_rules>>
    <<jump A1_Percival_Menu>>
-> Challenge him to a slam-off <<if flagged("a1_slam_rules") and not flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_1>>
-> Ask about his poetry <<if not flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Percival Thorne: My latest: "Ode to My Own Reflection." It's a trilogy.
    Percival Thorne: "O mirror, mirror, thin and wide, how lucky you are to see me from outside."
    Dex: (That was horrible. Ivy's poem is a thousand times better.)
    <<jump A1_Percival_Menu>>
-> Tell him the notebook is Ivy's <<if flagged("a1_heard_notebook") and not flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Percival Thorne: Ivy? The girl who never talks? Then she won't complain, will she?
    Dex: (Oh, I am going to beat this guy.)
    <<jump A1_Percival_Menu>>
-> Ask how he's doing <<if flagged("a1_won_slam")>>
    Percival Thorne: Fine. Great. Writing a poem about it. It's called "Nobody Asked You, Dex." It's mostly crying.
    <<jump A1_Percival_Menu>>
-> Leave
    Percival Thorne: Exit, stage left. Snap snap.
===
title: A1_Slam_1
---
Percival Thorne: (snaps fingers) Slam-off! Round one!
Percival Thorne: "I know forty thousand words, freshman!"
<<flag a1_ins1>>
-> "Shame the only one you ever use is 'me'." <<if flagged("a1_cb_me")>>
    Percival Thorne: (staggering) Gah. That... was rude. And accurate. Round two!
    <<jump A1_Slam_2>>
-> "So does onion soup, and it has more layers." <<if flagged("a1_cb_onion")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "So is the puddle on the library steps, and it shows more reflection." <<if flagged("a1_cb_puddle")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "People can't look away from car crashes either." <<if flagged("a1_cb_crash")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "Cool story. Tell it to my pillow." <<if flagged("a1_cb_pillow")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "Oh yeah? Well... I know some words too."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "I'm rubber, you're glue."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
===
title: A1_Slam_2
---
Percival Thorne: "My poems make grown men weep!"
<<flag a1_ins2>>
-> "Shame the only one you ever use is 'me'." <<if flagged("a1_cb_me")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "So does onion soup, and it has more layers." <<if flagged("a1_cb_onion")>>
    Percival Thorne: (clutching his scarf) Onion soup?! How DARE you compare me to a... delicious soup. Round three!
    <<jump A1_Slam_3>>
-> "So is the puddle on the library steps, and it shows more reflection." <<if flagged("a1_cb_puddle")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "People can't look away from car crashes either." <<if flagged("a1_cb_crash")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "Cool story. Tell it to my pillow." <<if flagged("a1_cb_pillow")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "Yeah, because they have to listen to them."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "I'm rubber, you're glue."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
===
title: A1_Slam_3
---
Percival Thorne: "My verse is far too deep for the likes of you!"
<<flag a1_ins3>>
-> "Shame the only one you ever use is 'me'." <<if flagged("a1_cb_me")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "So does onion soup, and it has more layers." <<if flagged("a1_cb_onion")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "So is the puddle on the library steps, and it shows more reflection." <<if flagged("a1_cb_puddle")>>
    Percival Thorne: (gasping) A puddle! With... more reflection than me?! Ms. Hush has been talking. Final round!
    <<jump A1_Slam_4>>
-> "People can't look away from car crashes either." <<if flagged("a1_cb_crash")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "Cool story. Tell it to my pillow." <<if flagged("a1_cb_pillow")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "I can swim, you know."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "I'm rubber, you're glue."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
===
title: A1_Slam_4
---
Percival Thorne: (shaking) "When I perform, nobody can take their eyes off me!"
<<flag a1_ins4>>
-> "Shame the only one you ever use is 'me'." <<if flagged("a1_cb_me")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "So does onion soup, and it has more layers." <<if flagged("a1_cb_onion")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "So is the puddle on the library steps, and it shows more reflection." <<if flagged("a1_cb_puddle")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "People can't look away from car crashes either." <<if flagged("a1_cb_crash")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Win>>
-> "Cool story. Tell it to my pillow." <<if flagged("a1_cb_pillow")>>
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "That's because your scarf is blinding."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
-> "I'm rubber, you're glue."
    <<jump A1_Slam_Lose>>
===
title: A1_Slam_Lose
---
Percival Thorne: Ha! Weak! Limp! Is that a comeback or a cry for help? The champion remains the champion!
<<flag a1_lost_slam>>
Dex: That didn't land. I need the RIGHT answer for each of his put-downs.
Dex: People around campus say clever things all the time. I should listen, and remember.
===
title: A1_Slam_Win
---
Percival Thorne: (falling into a beanbag) A car crash. He called me a car crash. And he was RIGHT.
Percival Thorne: Thirty-seven and... one. Take it. Take the notebook. Take my dignity while you're at it.
Dex: I'll just take the notebook. You can keep the dignity. What's left of it.
<<give ivy_notebook>>
<<flag a1_won_slam>>
===
title: A1_Percival_ShowHat
---
Percival Thorne: A cowboy hat? Is this a costume party? I don't slam against cosplayers.
===
title: A1_Percival_ShowNote
---
Percival Thorne: "Circle YES or YES." Derivative. Also, coercive. Also... oddly charming. Go away.
===

title: Item_ivy_notebook_Look
---
Dex: Ivy's notebook. A daisy doodled on the cover, and "Ode to the Quiet Kid in the Back Row" inside. Percival's name is crossed out. Good.
===
